      "lineNbr": 502,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-09T23:32:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yup. In that case, `init_and_wait` will fail after 1s as initial PPM reset didn\u0027t succeed. PPM_RESET should always succeed unless there is something wrong w/ the PDC itself (or I2C) and the only recovery for that is probably a power cutoff reset. \n\nBy design, the policy only applies on a successful ppm reset (meaning previous policies were removed).",
      "parentUuid": "2cebd51f_b4272506",
      "revId": "87117557f37a22aebeff5d0be5e4fb48951f8f1c",
